    {
      "bbox": [
        190,
        733,
        1497,
        925
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, on October 6, 2022, New York State enacted legislation (Chapter 569 of 2022) that increased to $1,000,000 the dollar threshold for making noncompetitive small purchases of goods, services and construction from City-certified Minority and Women-Owned Businesses (\"M/WBEs\") to address the continuing effects of discrimination against M/WBEs in the market where the City conducts its procurements; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.3257,
          "min": -1.6001
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0002,
          "min": -0.0002
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 100,
          "mean": -0.0015,
          "min": -0.1286
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 37526,
        "area_px": 245626,
        "density": 0.15278,
        "chars": 407,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 10.85
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        189,
        965,
        1491,
        1083
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, the City has established and implemented procedures to secure meaningful M/WBE participation and is committed to making New York City a more equitable and inclusive business environment for all vendors, including M/WBEs, to operate; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.2429,
          "min": -1.2673
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 46,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0019
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 22887,
        "area_px": 152439,
        "density": 0.15014,
        "chars": 245,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 10.7
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        187,
        1119,
        1491,
        1235
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, studies by the National Bureau of Economic Research and other institutions suggest that the economic and health effects of the COVID-19 pandemic have had a persistent and disproportionately negative impact on M/WBEs; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2235,
          "min": -1.3016
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 43,
          "mean": -0.0006,
          "min": -0.0264
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 21265,
        "area_px": 149877,
        "density": 0.14188,
        "chars": 229,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 10.77
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        187,
        1274,
        1489,
        1353
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, these studies also suggest that the negative impact is greater with respect to some ethnic and gender categories of M/WBEs than with respect to others; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2335,
          "min": -1.386
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
